From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:21:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: edit and delete a received message where it is, and
 show polls and contact cards as the app does

* Edit and delete a received message where it is

An edit or deletion from elsewhere was told with a notice under the
conversation ("X edited the message from T: new", "Message from T has
been deleted"), and only for a message shown in this session. The
Messaging app keeps every message, so it can show the change on the
message itself.

An edited text message now emits "webos-im-edit" (account,
"<chatId>:<messageId>", text as markup), and each permanently deleted
message emits "webos-im-delete" (account, "<chatId>:<messageId>"),
whichever session the message came in. imlibpurpleservice finds the
stored message by that id, as it does for Discord. A text edit needs
nothing fetched any more and gets no notice; a caption or a replaced
file is still told with a notice, as before. Deletions no longer get a
notice. This is for the Messaging app only (isWebosUi()): other
front-ends are told with the notices as before.

webosServiceMessageId() makes the id in one place; the reply quote, the
reactions and the outbox id use it too. The test mock keeps the two
signals for the tests to check.

* Show a received poll and contact card as the Messaging app does

Both came in as "Unsupported message type" with TDLib's description of
them. The Messaging app has a bubble for each, and purple-combined
(WhatsApp) already gives them in its forms:

- a poll is a "poll:<base64url JSON>" token, {"name", "options", "max"}
  with max 1 for one answer and 0 for any number, which the app draws
  as a list to vote on. A vote from it comes as
  "webos-im-send-poll-vote" (account, peer, "<chatId>:<messageId>",
  option texts "\x1f"-joined); the plug-in gets the poll to learn its
  options' positions and sends setPollAnswer. None chosen takes the vote
  back. A failure is told in the chat.
- a contact card is written as contact_<sha256>.vcf next to the files
  TDLib downloads, its vCard as it came or one made from the name and
  number, and shown as "file://<path>?name=<name>", which the app offers
  to import into Contacts. Where it cannot be written the name and
  number are shown as text.

Locations were already shown with their geo: link.

The forms are in webos-receive.cpp, the vote's option positions in
webos-send.cpp, with unit tests.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
